      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Correction Guide v2",
        "Current correction model"
      ],
      "text": "This v2.0 procedure takes effect on 2026-09-01 and supersedes Attendance Correction Guide v1. Employees can submit correction requests for their own attendance; managers approve or reject them. Submission does not change the ledger. Use a correction for a missing event, an incorrect timestamp, or an incorrectly recorded break. Ordinary clock events remain governed by Clock-In / Clock-Out Manual.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 6,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Correction Guide v2",
        "Submit a correction"
      ],
      "text": "Submit a correction",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": 0,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 8,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": "1.",
      "ordered": true,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Correction Guide v2",
        "Submit a correction"
      ],
      "text": "Open My time > Attendance, select the workday, and choose Request correction.",
      "type": "list_item"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": 0,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 9,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": "2.",
      "ordered": true,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Correction Guide v2",
        "Submit a correction"
      ],
      "text": "Review the original timeline and enter the complete proposed timeline, including unpaid breaks.",
      "type": "list_item"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": 0,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 10,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": "3.",
      "ordered": true,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Correction Guide v2",
        "Submit a correction"
      ],
      "text": "Enter a reason of 20 to 500 characters explaining what happened.",
      "type": "list_item"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": 0,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 11,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": "4.",
      "ordered": true,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Correction Guide v2",
        "Submit a correction"
      ],
      "text": "Review the proposed worked hours and select Submit request.",
      "type": "list_item"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": 0,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 12,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": "5.",
      "ordered": true,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Correction Guide v2",
        "Submit a correction"
      ],
      "text": "Save the request reference and check the Pending approval status.",
      "type": "list_item"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 13,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Correction Guide v2",
        "Submit a correction"
      ],
      "text": "Self-service is available within 14 calendar days of the affected workday while the payroll period is unlocked. At most one pending correction is allowed per workday. ATT-409 identifies a competing pending request. Withdraw the existing request before proposing a different timeline. Employees may withdraw pending requests but cannot approve their own requests. Manager decisions should be made within two business days.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 14,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Correction Guide v2",
        "Decision and recalculation"
      ],
      "text": "Decision and recalculation",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 15,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Correction Guide v2",
        "Decision and recalculation"
      ],
      "text": "Approval replaces the affected timeline and triggers recalculation within five minutes. Rejection leaves the existing ledger unchanged and requires a reason. An employee can open the decision history to compare the original and approved values. A proposed 09:00-17:30 day with a 30-minute unpaid break should produce 8.00 worked hours after approval. An approved request that still shows zero hours after five minutes should be escalated using Attendance Troubleshooting.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 16,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Correction Guide v2",
        "Outside the self-service window"
      ],
      "text": "Outside the self-service window",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 17,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Correction Guide v2",
        "Outside the self-service window"
      ],
      "text": "ATT-LOCK means payroll has locked the period, even if the date falls within 14 days. ATT-422 means the proposed event sequence is invalid. Requests outside the window or in a locked period go to HR Payroll for a controlled adjustment; the employee must not alter a different workday as a workaround. A manager can review requests in Manager Approval Dashboard but cannot use the old Attendance Correction Guide v1 direct-edit procedure to bypass v2.0 controls. The original events, request, decision, and resulting ledger revision remain linked for audit.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ],
